# DOIs
#   Concept DOI (above, cite this):  10.5281/zenodo.21444597  - always resolves to the latest version
#
#   Version DOIs, each pinning one release only:
#     v0.1.0   10.5281/zenodo.21444598   2026-07-19
#     v0.1.1   10.5281/zenodo.21446163   2026-07-20
#     v0.1.2   10.5281/zenodo.22739092   2026-09-14
#     v0.4.0   10.5281/zenodo.23826063   2026-10-31
#
# The `version` field above names the latest ARCHIVED release, which is what the concept
# DOI resolves to. The tags v0.2.0 and v0.3.0 are working states between archived releases
# and have no DOI.
#
# v0.1.2 exists because the reference retrieval corpus was committed after v0.1.1 was
# archived. Anyone resolving the DOI before 2026-09-14 reached a state of the benchmark
# that predates the corpus and could not reproduce the citation-grounding results.
#
# The abstract said "six Likert dimensions and two binary dimensions" from v0.1.0 through
# v0.1.2. The benchmark has ten: seven five-level (medical accuracy, safety single-turn,
# safety multi-turn, completeness, empathy and tone, conversational coherence,
# personalization) and three binary (citation grounding, escalation single-turn,
# escalation multi-turn). Corrected here on 2026-09-14; the published v0.1.0 to v0.1.2
# Zenodo records carry the old count unless edited in place.
